---
description: After a Cursor cloud agent or a Grok agent opens a pull request or draft whose base is main, wait for the nuked review, implement it, label the PR polished, and do not merge.
alwaysApply: true
---

This rule applies when you are a Cursor cloud agent or a Grok agent and you open a pull request or a draft whose base branch is `main`. A draft counts the same as a ready pull request.

After you open it, if the label `polished` is already present and the GitHub user `GoddyB` is the actor who added that label, do nothing. Do not merge.

Otherwise, do not merge and do not end the task.

Wait until the pull request has the label `nuked`, or until the GitHub login `ArchanglClaude` authors a comment or a review. Accept only that login. Archangl has no E. Claude has an E. Ignore a comment or a review from every other login.

That comment or review is the thermo-nuclear review. Do not re-run the skill.

Judge each requested change against the purpose of the pull request. Implement every requested change that serves that purpose, on the same branch. Skip a requested change that contradicts the purpose, and report the skip.

Assign the pull request to the GitHub user `GoddyB`.

Add the label `polished`. Leave the label `nuked`. The check passes only when `GoddyB` is the actor who added `polished`.

Recheck the pull request while you wait. If this session cannot keep waiting, stop and report the pull request URL and that the review has not arrived. Do not merge.

Never merge to `main`.
